  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project on Agricultural Value Chain Enhancement for Women Economic Empowerment in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the Integrated Household Living Conditions Survey (EICV, 2018) conducted by the Rwandan government, Rwanda&apos;s poverty rate in 2016-2017 was 38.2% and extreme poverty rate was 16%. In Rwanda, immediately after the 1994 genocide, more than 70% of the adult population became women due to the deaths of many men, which increased women&apos;s economic responsibilities. Nevertheless, it was found that women&apos;s occupational diversity and self-reliance capabilities were still lower than those of men.&#xbe48;&#xace4; &#xc5ec;&#xc131; &#xb18d;&#xc5c5;&#xac00;&#xce58;&#xc0ac;&#xc2ac; &#xb300;&#xc751; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9; &#xac15;&#xd654;,&#xc5ec;&#xc131;&#xc758; &#xacbd;&#xc81c; &#xc0ac;&#xd68c; &#xd65c;&#xb3d9; &#xcc38;&#xc5ec; &#xc99d;&#xc9c4;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing accessibility to agricultural technology,Creation of foundation for value chain participation,Improving financial accessibility,Promoting Women Social Integration</narrative>
  </description>
